I've played a lot of from software game  demos over the years and every demo is  better than the last but cicchitto is in  a different category entirely this game  is seven whole months away from release  and yet every input felt responsive  every death felt deserved except this  one and I swear I didn't fall below 60  frames per second a single time this  game has so much potential and I mean  you could see it in the faces of people  around me playing at Gamescom I watched  other people play when I got the chance  and almost without fail everyone did the  same thing at the start they see this  green don't slide into view and then  they use their grappling hook over and  over again just speeding between  rooftops and branches because you feel  it right away freedom you realize that  in all the souls games prior to this the  environments have controlled you they  restricted you they guided you but now  you control the environment  it's your weapon to use against your  enemies it's your safe space to retreat  and to heal it's always like a jump or  just a grapple away and it's yours in an  instant that sense of control is what  differentiates cicchitto in my opinion  from every souls like game before it and  that grappling hook is just one small  part of that control because what's even  more important is how responsive the  character feels take this scene for  example it's a good one think about all  the inputs I'm putting in here I managed  to jump off this ledge turn on a dime in  midair  lock-on and initiate a plunging attack  on the soldier below me my character  just responded to a ton of button inputs  and as I continued playing it felt like  the only thing really holding me back  were my own reflexes that sense of  control is what differentiates sukira  from every souls like game before it in  my opinion  another example is here when the  trol holds me off a cliff it was a  really embarrassing moment because I was  toying with him and just watching him  take burn damage but you see that green  marker if I had pressed l2 at this  moment I'm pretty sure I could have  grappled back up to the troll and man if  that had happened I would be showing you  an incredible clip instead of an  embarrassing one but I am getting ahead  of myself before I was thrown off this  cliff I had to kill a ton of human  enemies to get here so let's go over the  combat and how I fought my way to this  point  so first cicchitto has incredibly fast  to recovery times there's barely any  delay between attacking blocking and  dodging which when you think about it is  really different from souls because in  souls you're forced to commit to long  animations and long attacks but in  cicchitto your animation sequencing is  rapid and your reflexes take the center  stage this leads us to the posture  system in cicchitto you have no stamina  actually better way of saying that is  probably that you have infinite stamina  so this enables you and your enemies to  attack sprint block and roll to your  heart's content  but it comes at a price because instead  of stamina the resource you're managing  is called posture and at the bottom of  the screen now you can see my posture  and atop my enemy's heads you can see  their posture or if there are mini buffs  you can see it at the top in the middle  of the screen the goal is to completely  fill an enemy's posture bar which then  knocks them off balance and enables a  critical attack you can fill their bar  in two ways first you can test their  defenses by attacking them with our one  or you can parry their attacks  there is no parry button mind you you  just have to press the block button in  the instant they would have hit you the  better you time it the more they're  knocked off balance and the worst you  time it you won't take health damage but  you will take a big posture hit so  always remember the  same rules apply to your character  except when your posture is broken your  character gets knocked to the floor  instead of being critically attacked and  when you see this neon pink Japanese  character for danger pop up that means  the incoming attack can't be blocked  instead you can - or you can jump out of  the way  and yeah there's actually two separate  dodge buttons this time around so - is  your faster option it's what you're  already familiar with but sometimes you  actually need to jump over an enemies  attack instead now jump is much slower  but you can block and you can also  attack while you're jumping in the  middle of your jump which is amazing for  how fluid it makes the game feel you can  even jump off of enemies heads and  double jump on walls and all kinds of  crazy stuff so yeah you get the hang of  this pretty quick it took me about 15  minutes before I stopped floundering and  actually started playing well but as you  can probably tell this is far more  complex than any game that came before  it in my opinion I'm really curious to  see what the community thinks because  it's pretty unique to have to manage  your health and your posture and then  also on top of that manage whether  you're supposed to jump or - out of the  way when an enemy is attacking you  there's a lot of micromanagement in  cicchitto and it's fast-paced on top of  that so yeah mismanaging anything could  instantly lead to your death  but then one death doesn't matter that  much in cicchitto does it you see that  pink token in the bottom left above our  health that token represents  resurrection and pressing your right  bumper after death allows you to consume  it and come back to life now if you do  enough damage after your resurrection  you can actually earn this token back  which allows you to resurrect a second  time and if you do enough damage after  that you can resurrect a third time and  so on and so forth  I assume of all the systems from  software has repeatedly stated that  they're really tweaking the resurrection  mechanic to get it feeling right and I  have to wonder if there's a limit to how  many times you can resurrect I think  personally the max I got was three  before I died permanently so yeah I  guess shadows can die more than twice  and we've yet to see how many times  often you'll die in a position which  enables your stealth a Crouch which is  enabled when you press l3 so while  you're undetected you can of course  initiate a critical strike whenever you  see that glowing red lock-on icon and if  you're lucky enough to find some tall  grass you're pretty much completely  invisible as far as I can tell as long  as you don't enter the grass with a  weapon that's on fire because if you do  then it will set the whole field ablaze  and I did not expect that that's  something I can definitely see them  incorporating into like a boss fight  imagine hiding in the grass and then  having enemies trying to burn you out I  think that'd be awesome my flaming sword  speaking of which was enabled with a  prosthetic combo so prosthetic combos  are when you use your prosthetic trick  weapon and combo it with an r1 attack  with  Kitana and this is a mechanic that you  do not want to underestimate it's so  powerful so there were three prosthetic  weapons that you could use in this demo  there was the flame cannon the shrew  canal and the hand axe and prosthetic  attacks consumed white spirit emblems  which is a resource that you get from  enemies and it's displayed down there in  the bottom right as I mentioned you can  combo your prosthetics with r1 to  basically double their effectiveness the  flame cannon  for example combos to buff your sword  with fire the shrew can arm combo is  fantastic way better than I expected it  pegs a shuriken and then it closes the  gap with your katana in an instant and  the hair backs combo is basically an  instant kill on any smaller enemy it  obliterates their posture and enables a  critical attack and one touch that I  love is that enemies now jump back in  fear when they see you performing a  takedown on one of their allies and I  don't blame them because some of these  executions are brutal and guys I could  honestly talk about my experience hours  and I might honestly do that when I get  home I might stream this and talk about  all the footage in crazy high detail but  right now it's 3 a.m. in my hotel I  still have to edit all this together and  my microphone is failing me so I think  I've explained everything that needs  explaining and I kind of expect you'll  be able to puzzle out the rest from all  the footage I'll be providing and it's  hard for me to express this without  sounding generic but there is so much I  haven't talked about there are a couple  of incredible bosses that I'm not even  allowed to talk about and I wish I could  rave about every little detail about  this demo with you in person because  I've been lucky enough to have that  experience with a couple of guys here at  Gamescom and it's so much fun talking  about this game with other people who  enjoy it as much as you do if there are  any gaming conventions near you and the  next few months I would highly recommend  you check if secure oh is one of the  games that you can play there it  one of the most polished demos are  played in my life but before I go I  absolutely have to give special thanks  to Activision who made it well worth it  for me to fly halfway across the world  just to get some cicchitto footage and  talk about it with you guys thanks  especially to Joanna  Alexis Allison Tom and Priya they're the  reason this video exists and I'm hugely  thankful it's been a hell of an  experience I will have one more video on  sukira to work on when I get home I  think  but until then thank you so much for  watching check out the other sticky tour  video which is basically just all my  footage with all the raw music and  sounds and everything without me talking  over it in a tired voice but until next  time guys thanks for watching and I'll  see that
 

